Z||000000||wxxo||03-28-2000||02:49 PM||||i got in my 86se v6 4spd this morning and started it up. thats when the problems began. one of the belts started squeaking really bad and when i got it out onto the road all of the idiot gauges started going haywire. the battery meter had been slightly in the red for a few days now and the oil pressuse has been really high as well(better high than low though.) id say around the last mark on the readout. anyone got any ideas?? i must say though that since the battery guage has been in the red it has a lot more power. strange. anyhow tia for the help.||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||03-28-2000||03:24 PM||||Alternator going bad is my guess. Could explain the squealing belt, guage problems, power changes, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ironhorse||03-28-2000||04:14 PM||||wxxo, I agree with Fiero56.  I would have the alternator checked out immediately.  It sounds like from what you've said that it's overcharging, BAD BAD BAD expecially for ecm, and other electrical components that's in Fiero.  Take it out and go to Autozone or someplace that will test it for ya.||||reg||1
Z||000003||wxxo||03-28-2000||04:54 PM||||thanks guys...thats what ill do. now for another question. is the alternator in my car going to be difficult to get out?? i thought that i could work on cars until i got this thing. everything is bachwards. anyhow...how much time do you think that it will take to get that thing out of there?? got a hanes so that will help i guess. thanks again.||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||03-28-2000||06:08 PM||||You've got be nimble if you're going to do it from the top.  The manual says to remove the splash guard, but I didn't do that.  If you loosen the bottom bolt, it relieves the stress from the belt. The top one is pretty easy.  From there, I was able to drop mine out from the bottom.  Not too bad.||||reg||1
